  "rationale": "D4 of the hinge-law spec for normal flames, data-informed (not zero-shot): D3 with two statements corrected that stood on mis-tabulated train rows. The levelling off of the butane dilution penalty below 12 % is removed (the flames it was typed from burned 30 % butane, not 3 %). Butane is shorter than ethane in air as well as in enriched oxygen (-0.2 at any oxygen; the flames that seemed to be on the ethane law in air burned 0.49 to 0.66 mg/s, not 0.8), with the oxygen slope lowered so that the term at 39 % oxygen is unchanged. Nothing else is changed. Every number typed by the author; no fit, no search; nothing chosen from validation.",
  "origin": "system"
